# Notepad File > Save As (COMMDLG): the file names grey, a name that is not valid ("a,b\nThis filename is
# not valid.") and an existing file with the overwrite prompt, answered No (the fixture's SETUP.TXT is a
# link to the user's ripped file: never answer Yes here). Reference: arch311-ref scn/cdlg-save.scn (frame
# 01 is Notepad before the scenario starts). The recorder kept the edit part way through typing
# "setup.txt" ("setup.t"), so the script shoots there too.
# regress: sh tools/run-fixture-test.sh notepad "$TEST" "$OUT"
# compare: cdlg-save/02.png 01-saveas.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: cdlg-save/03.png 02-typed.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: cdlg-save/04.png 03-box.png ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: cdlg-save/07.png 06-prompt.png ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: cdlg-save/05.png 04-back.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: cdlg-save/06.png 05-typed.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: cdlg-save/08.png 07-back.png active ignore 320 240 332 260
# compare: cdlg-save/09.png 08-closed.png active ignore 316 228 333 261
sleep 400
type Hello
key alt+f
key a
sleep 400
shotcaret shots/01-saveas.png
type a,b
sleep 400
shot shots/02-typed.png
key enter
sleep 400
shot shots/03-box.png
key enter
sleep 400
shotcaret shots/04-back.png
type setup.t
sleep 400
shotcaret shots/05-typed.png
type xt
key enter
sleep 400
shot shots/06-prompt.png
key n
sleep 400
shotcaret shots/07-back.png
key esc
sleep 400
shotcaret shots/08-closed.png
quit
